LAN (OSPF) < WAN (BGP): outage cause of overwelming number of routes (bad but not causeable)
LAN (OSPF) > WAN (BGP): possible route redirection via route redistribution

OSPF to BGP route redistribution done via 3 ways:
1) share via OSPF processes (all areas in an area, basically everything)
2) share via OSPG processes including external routes
3) share via route maps (basically ACLs for routes)

