BGP
basic operation:
ASN manually configured, eBGP and IBGP are deteremined if the router and its neighbor is the same or different respectively
open messages share the ASN of the router
BGP neighbors must be configured with both IP and ASN, unless the configuration is done with a dynamic bgp range config which allows ip of a range to be associated with an ASN 
the BGP types are session-based/link-based not router global
may assign its own attributes to the route (not carrying over bogus tags)
OSPF routes will be marked as Incomplete whereas IGP will be marked as such (a marked origin will be preferred to an incomplete one)

